+# Changelog
+
+All notable changes to this project are documented here.
+
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Added
+- README: project origin note and project history section (rehearsal version vs portfolio version).
+- This changelog.
+
+### Planned
+- LLM-based invoice extraction with schema-constrained output and deterministic validation.
+- Published evaluation scorecard on the 50-invoice synthetic corpus.
+- Testcontainers-based integration tests and a cleaned-up migration history.
+- Decision (ADR) on whether a durable processing queue is needed.
+- CI/CD and hosted deployment.
+
+## [rehearsal-v0] - 2026-10-22
+
+Snapshot of the project as built as a **dress rehearsal for the Accel Hackathon Paris** (commits from 2026-10-21 to 2026-10-22, last commit `f2d417f`).
+
+### Included
+- Cookie-based authentication with demonstration bootstrap credentials.
+- Secure PDF upload and storage, document listing and download.
+- PostgreSQL persistence with EF Core migrations.
+- React review interface with correction and approve/reject flows.
+- Synthetic 50-invoice ground-truth corpus and prediction scoring harness.
+- Docker Compose setup and GitHub Actions CI.
+
+### Known gaps at the time
+- No working end-to-end extraction: extractor methods unimplemented, no external AI client.
+- Worker and durable queue incomplete.
+- Integration tests use mocks only.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index cc97906..140ff8d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,23 @@
 
 An ASP.NET Core and React prototype for storing invoice PDFs and reviewing extracted invoice data. The repository contains parts of an invoice-processing architecture, but it is **not yet a working end-to-end AI extraction system**. The current state and limitations are described below so that demo results are not confused with live model output.
 
+> **Project origin:** this project started as a **dress rehearsal for the Accel Hackathon Paris**: a prototype built beforehand to prepare (commits from 21–22 October 2026). It is not the hackathon entry itself. The state at the end of the rehearsal is preserved as the [`rehearsal-v0`](https://github.com/SDormans/DocumentProcessing/releases/tag/rehearsal-v0) release and tag. Work after that point is being done deliberately in the open, as a portfolio project, and is tracked in the [changelog](CHANGELOG.md). See [Project history](#project-history).
+<!-- TODO: credit teammates here if the rehearsal was done as a team. -->
+
+## Project history
+
+| | Rehearsal version (`rehearsal-v0`) | Portfolio version (in progress) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Goal | Prepare for the Accel Hackathon Paris with an invoice-processing prototype | Turn the prototype into a working, measured, tested project |
+| Upload, storage, review UI | Working | Working |
+| AI extraction | Not implemented end to end | Planned: LLM extraction with schema-constrained output and deterministic validation |
+| Evaluation | Harness and 50-invoice synthetic corpus, no model results | Planned: published scorecard with accuracy, latency and cost per invoice |
+| Integration tests | Controller-level, mocked | Planned: real PostgreSQL via Testcontainers |
+| Background processing | Incomplete worker and queue | Planned: decide with an ADR whether a durable queue is justified |
+| Deployment | Local Docker Compose only | Planned: CI/CD and a hosted deployment |
+
+Everything in the right-hand column marked "Planned" is not done yet. This README will be updated as each item lands, and the sections below describe the **current** state of the repository, including its known limitations.
+
 ## What works today
 
 - Cookie-based sign-in with configurable demonstration bootstrap credentials.
